From 6c48d98ccb39ac35337c0ef995fcb14b7db6f2e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:08:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] dsv41: TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2_NORM (off by default): the
 ratio-2 compressor chain and the RMSNorm in one launch

TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2_NORM gates one launch for the ratio-2 compressor chain and the RMSNorm after
it, off by default, on both call sites: decode (round.zig's compressorChain) and prompt (prompt.zig's
ratio-2 branch). The decode kernel replicates the 0127 fusion's scatter/gather/compress2 arithmetic
verbatim and then the kit's `_rmsnorm` (BLOCK = pow2(D), num_warps = 4; tl.sum's order reconstructed
as per-thread sequential over EPT contiguous elements, a butterfly xor 16..1 across the warp, then a
4-lane butterfly over the warp partials - the honest reduction-order risk, gated on the Spark exact
suite). The prompt kernel reproduces tf_ds_compress2_kernel and tf_ds_rms_norm_kernel (torch's
arithmetic and reduce order, already bit-checked against torch on GB10). Both call sites gate on
fuseOk: a shape the kernels do not take runs the unfused launches instead. Precedence:
TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2_NORM wins over TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2 (it implies that fusion); 0127 alone
keeps its behaviour; neither = the unfused chain. The one-row prompt chunk (full == 0) returns
before any launch, as before. UNVERIFIED-BUILD on this machine (no nvcc): gated on the exact suite on
a Spark like the rest of the series. ~3 launches a round saved; worth keeping only if TF_DS_PDL shows
real device-side gaps.
